    /* ── Reflections ── */
    'reflex.hero.breadcrumb':   'Reflections',
    'reflex.hero.tag':          'Reflections · Mindset · Journey',
    'reflex.hero.title':        'My honest reflections<br>on <em>money and investing</em>',
    'reflex.meta.readTime':     ' 6 min read',
    'reflex.meta.tags':         'Mindset · Income · Journey',
    'reflex.lead':              '"There\'s no single model for success. Everyone moves at their own pace. The important thing is to start somewhere."',
    'reflex.p1':                'My reflections come largely from my personal experience. Some people may recognize themselves completely in my journey, others less so — and that\'s perfectly normal. But I genuinely believe that everyone can take a small part of my story and adapt it to their own reality.',
    'reflex.h2.education':      'Education and skills — my first lever',
    'reflex.p2':                'One thing I find particularly important is <strong>education and developing your skills</strong>. Not everyone wants to become an entrepreneur, and that\'s not necessarily the right path for everyone. But today, in 2026, I believe it has become essential to find ways to increase your income or develop expertise that opens more doors.',
    'reflex.insight1.title':    'Going back to school — an investment in itself',
    'reflex.insight1.desc':     'Myself, after several years as a consultant, I asked: what could open even more possibilities for me? That\'s what pushed me to consider an IT college certificate — to acquire new skills and offer more services.',
    'reflex.insight2.title':    'A specialized skill changes everything',
    'reflex.insight2.desc':     'People who hold a professional license or offer specialized services often manage to earn a higher income. Insurance, finance, technology, consulting — these are the skills that give more financial flexibility.',
    'reflex.h2.small':          'Even $20 can make a difference',
    'reflex.p3':                'We often tend to underestimate small amounts. But when you develop <strong>the habit of saving regularly</strong>, even modestly, it can change many things in the long run — obviously, when your financial situation allows it.',
    'reflex.pullquote':         '"I prefer to work hard now while I have the energy, so I can be more at ease later."',
    'reflex.h2.income':         'Multiple income streams — my reality',
    'reflex.p4':                'Today, I think having a <strong>single income source</strong> can be difficult for many people, especially with today\'s cost of living. When you\'re on your own or don\'t have a very high salary, saving can become a real challenge.',
    'reflex.p5':                'What helped me a lot was <strong>offering services alongside my main job</strong>. I\'ve worked for employers, but I\'ve also developed my own projects and worked with my own clients. This allowed me to supplement my income while maintaining a certain quality of life.',
    'reflex.highlight':         'I\'m not saying it\'s easy. It takes time, energy and discipline. But I\'ve always had this mindset: <strong>work hard now to be more at ease later.</strong> And invest every extra dollar earned — even $20 — rather than spending it.',
    'reflex.h2.wealth':         'What I learned about wealth',
    'reflex.insight3.title':    'Time is the real capital',
    'reflex.insight3.desc':     'Money invested early is worth much more than money invested late. Every year you wait costs tens of thousands of dollars in the long run.',
    'reflex.insight4.title':    'Start small, stay consistent',
    'reflex.insight4.desc':     '$50 every two weeks for 20 years can become more than $100,000. It\'s not the amount that matters — it\'s the consistency.',
    'reflex.insight5.title':    'Mindset first',
    'reflex.insight5.desc':     'See every expense as a conscious choice. Every dollar not invested today is several dollars lost in 20 years.',
    'reflex.h2.final':          'In the end',
    'reflex.p6':                'I believe there is no single model for success. Everyone moves at their own pace. The important thing is to <strong>start somewhere</strong>, stay consistent and gradually build a life that brings more stability, freedom and peace of mind.',
    'reflex.p7':                'This blog is my journey — imperfect, honest, human. If a single idea here helps you take one step toward a better financial situation, that\'s all I hope for.',
    'reflex.disclaimer':        ' I am not a financial advisor. This article shares my personal experience and reflections — not official financial advice.',
    'reflex.sidebar.title':     'Start investing',
    'reflex.sidebar.body':      'Even with $50. Wealthsimple — free, no commission.',
